#: ../../004_cli_tool.md:593
msgid "Logging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../004_cli_tool.md:595
msgid ""
"When a script is executed (not in `--dry-run` mode), the CLI "
"automatically creates a log file next to the script at "
"`<script_name>.log`. For example, running `my_script.yaml` produces "
"`my_script.log` in the same directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../004_cli_tool.md:597
msgid "**Log level**: INFO and above (INFO, WARNING, ERROR)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../004_cli_tool.md:598
msgid "**Encoding**: UTF-8"
msgstr ""

#: ../../004_cli_tool.md:599
msgid ""
"**Lifecycle**: The log file is created when execution begins and the log "
"sink is removed when execution completes (regardless of success or "
"failure). If the log file already exists, it is overwritten."
msgstr ""

#: ../../004_cli_tool.md:601
msgid ""
"This log file captures the same structured messages shown in the console "
"output, providing a persistent record of script execution for debugging "
"and auditing."
msgstr ""

